  "scope": "# Review \u2014 1856980929fe\nTask/source: `1856980929fe`, generator `3.0.0`, final SHA-256 `cf6e08b5e647f09dd3011b3d7ad3652e37df3f7ec354a7a1ba07bb570df22636`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: a five-demo lesson could hide a third query seed; added executable `first_two_seeds_only` rival plus `third_seed_expansion` witness and gate binding.\nCounterexample: seed 2/easy, demos 11\u201315 have seed counts `1,1,2,2,2`; query 16 has 3 and is changed by the rival.\nGate check: 300 raw lessons exposed 7 query-changing survivors; the repaired `lesson_identifiable` rejected all 7, zero missed (`checks/repair/1856980929fe-first-two-gate-v1.json`).\nCanonical rule: unchanged; normalized rule hash remains `77504f6c55fa`; sampler `VERSION` remains `3.0.0` to avoid keyed-RNG schedule drift.\nParametric proposal: episode-fixed `fan_stride \u2208 {1,2}` under `workspace/parametric/`; stride 1 is byte-identical to canonical Racket source.\nParameter evidence: 2 episodes, 3 demos + 4 distinct queries each, exact Racket labels, both alternative settings refuted, independent replay PASS (`checks/parametric/1856980929fe-fan-stride-v1/`).\nChanged-scope tests: task-local suite PASS, 57 tests; focused prototype suite is included in that total.\nSupplementary tickets: pinned singleton-corner audit reproduced; peer `250a48232c34` silently accepts typo override `n_anchor` and needs maintainer attention.\nRemaining limits: finite seeds/lesson assembler only; prototype is unapproved and makes no catalog or training-admission change.\nDisposition: main repair is routine and source-bound; supplementary API-boundary finding needs attention.",
